================================================================================
ADVERSARIAL VERDICT SUMMARY (kind-pasteur-S2-wf)
================================================================================
RE-DERIVED FROM SCRATCH AND CONFIRMED:
1. Danger comb D_w (w==0 mod14): w teeth at k/w, each half-width 1/(14w), full
   width 1/(7w), density 1/7, meas(D_w)=1/7 EXACTLY. Between-teeth safe gap 6/(7w)->0.
2. meas(G_drop6)=7/858 EXACTLY (4 mouths: 2x 1/728 + 2x 5/1848). Matches canon.
3. LOAD-BEARING per-arc inequality cover_w(A) <= |A|/7 + 1/(7w): VERIFIED.
   Exhaustive exact worst-case (all rational arcs, w=14,28,84): max excess
   STRICTLY BELOW 1/(7w) (3/343<1/98 etc). Bound is sound, even conservative.
   Worst arc = single arc inside one tooth (cover=whole tooth=1/(7w)). 0 violations
   over 4798 random arcs + exhaustive grid.
4. Decoupling bound L >= (6/7)meas - r/(7w): 0 violations. For drop-6 (r=4, smallest
   meas) the bound is POSITIVE only for w>=572/7=81.7; below that, exact min L=
   1543/294294=0.00524 at w=98, still >0. So 'thin comb cannot cover fat G_C'
   GEOMETRY IS CORRECT, but the bound alone is vacuous for small w (must exact-check).
5. THM-525 baseline {1..11,13,84}: M=7/89 at 37/89, 84 binding at frac 82/89 (EDGE
   of section 0, NOT middle). Confirmed.
6. GAP-A: drop-6 + coordinated w minimizes at w=69, L=19/10626 > 1/1260. Confirmed.

ADVERSARIAL HUNT FOR meas(G_C) < 7/858: ZERO found over:
   - all 13 single-drops of {1..13}; all C(14,12) 2-drops of {1..14}
   - 833 mult-14 cores; 36425 mult-mixed cores; 40000 structured-pool cores
   - ~43000 random primitive 12-sets (speeds up to 300); greedy descent
   - 15000 near-covering random cores (max r=220 components, all large meas)
   #(meas(G_C)==0) = 0 in all searches.

WHAT SURVIVES: the geometry ('thin comb cannot erase fat G_C') is ARITHMETICALLY
CORRECT and the comb-coverage inequality is rigorously true. meas(G_C) is NEVER
observed below 7/858 and NEVER zero.
WHAT DOES NOT SURVIVE AS A PROOF: the uniform lower bound meas(G_C) >= 7/858 (or
any c>0) for ALL 12-subsets is EXACTLY OPEN-Q-108 -- still a CONJECTURE. The
'thin comb' intuition only works GIVEN meas(G_C) bounded below; the searches
support but do not prove that bound. The k>=3 coordinated-growing-speeds regime
is the genuine uncontrolled gap. NO COUNTEREXAMPLE, but NO PROOF.
